{
  "protocol_name": "Serial 1:10 dilution of culture in 0.9% saline",
  "description": "Makes a six-step 1:10 serial dilution (10^-1 to 10^-6) of an overnight culture in sterile 0.9% saline across columns 1-6 of a 96-well plate, with 8 replicate rows. Plating and colony counting happen off-deck.",
  "assumptions": [
    "The text says 1 mL culture in 10 mL solvent but calls it a 1:10 dilution. I kept the 1:10 dilution factor per step: 10 uL culture + 90 uL saline = 100 uL per well (the scaled version of 1 mL into 9 mL, the standard reading of a 1:10 dilution). If the literal 1:11 is wanted, change the diluent to 100 uL.",
    "Volumes scaled from bench mL to plate uL: 1 mL culture becomes 10 uL and 90 uL diluent per well, to fit a 289.7 uL PCR well and 300 uL tips.",
    "Six dilution wells (10^-1 to 10^-6) were chosen because the culture density is not given. Plate the well whose colony count falls in 10-100 CFU/mL, off-deck.",
    "Each transfer is preceded by a 50 uL mix in the source well, and each well keeps about 90 uL after transfer, well above the 30 uL minimum.",
    "Each transfer pass uses its own tip column (1 for diluent, 2 for culture and first transfer, 3-6 for the next transfers, 7 for the final mix), so each tip column is used once.",
    "The culture is held in a reservoir, not a tube, so all 8 channels can draw from it. Only 80 uL is needed; 1 mL is loaded as margin.",
    "Diluent (sterile 0.9% saline) is 4.32 mL in total (3 aspirations of 180 uL per channel), so 5 mL is loaded.",
    "Plating onto agar, incubation and colony counting are not done by the robot and are left out of the steps."
  ],
